	(text "Aiming for 680-700uF total capacitance\nfor around 50Hz cut-off.\n\nNote that it does not mean low frequencies\nwill be perceived significantly lower.\nThe damping factor below the cut-off is\nsignificantly reduced, which would create\nmore low end “bloom”, and more perceivable\ndeepness.\n\nMore caps are better to distribute current\n(make sure ESR is consistent so some caps\nare not overworking over others).\nThis way you would not need big current\nripple rating for the caps.\nSo you can use smaller values but put\na big grid of them, so the current is\ndistributed between all of them."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.306 64.262 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "02dded4d-757c-43cb-b89a-1543ec3260e8")
	)
	(text "\n--------------TODO-----------------\n\nYou should expect around 30W of power\nfor each amplifier channel into 4 ohms.\nThe idea is that all 4 are driving 4\nspeakers independently, so that you\nget enough power, while each individual\namps is not that powerful.\n\nEverything is designed around 4 ohms\nload. The impedance transformers are\nsupposed to keep that 4 ohms load\nconsistency regardless of actual\nspeaker load you connect it to.\n\nMind that older TDA2050 chips seem to\nbe rated for lower voltages, so that’s\nwhy I picked ±20V supply, because it\nseems I have the older model. Otherwise\nyou could power it from ±24V for more\noutput power, more headroom. Also be aware\nthat TDA2050 is obsolete, no longer\nmanufactured. There are a lot of fakes\nin the market."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 345.44 203.454 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "8cd8145d-88fd-47c7-91eb-0874c2cc61fe")
	)
	(text "Each cap ≥1.5 A @100 Hz.\nVerify LF frequency derating."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175.26 95.25 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d851c106-86e5-4eee-bf03-6c09104521d0")
	)
